# {{PROJECT}} · {{CLIENT}}

SFDX project that works with the **sdd-salesforce {{VERSION}}** method (a Claude Code plugin). These instructions apply
in this folder and everything below it; if a `CLAUDE.md` in a parent folder says otherwise, this one wins here. **They
hold no task status**: the status lives in [`docs/delivery-plan/status.md`](docs/delivery-plan/status.md).

The **method's rules are not in this file**: the plugin injects them at the start of every session, when it is
resumed, after it is compacted and in the first message of a session that does not have them yet, and they are
complete in the `sdd-salesforce:sdd-method` skill. **If you do not see the notice «[sdd-salesforce …] sdd project» in
your context (and you have not just bootstrapped the project in this session with `sdd-bootstrap`), the plugin is not
loaded: stop and say so before doing any work.**

## The project

- **Org:** **{{ORG}}**, the only one for this project (`org_alias` in `sdd.config.json`). It expires on
  **{{EXPIRY}}**. Every `sf` command that touches an org carries `--target-org {{ORG}}`.
- **Approver:** **{{APPROVER}}**. **Autonomy:** `{{AUTONOMY}}`. {{ESCALATION}}.
- **Planned areas:** {{AREAS}}.
<!-- if language -->
- **Document language:** `{{LANGUAGE}}` (`method.language`). Headings, fields, IDs, git tags and file names stay as
  in the templates.
<!-- end if -->
- **Adoption of the method and the project's choices:**
  [decision 001](knowledge/decisions/{{SEED}}).

## Reading order

1. [`docs/delivery-plan/handover.md`](docs/delivery-plan/handover.md): operational entry point and the last dated
   handover.
2. [`docs/delivery-plan/status.md`](docs/delivery-plan/status.md): the single source of truth for status; the
   orchestrator writes it.
3. `knowledge/`: `Active` decisions, gotchas and the specs for the scope you are about to touch (`read-knowledge`
   skill).
4. The delivery plan (`docs/delivery-plan/README.md`, `implementation/`, `integration.md`) and the latest environment
   inventory (`docs/baseline/environment-*.md`), once they exist.

## Communication

- **Allowed channels:** {{CHANNELS}}.
- Every external message, even an acknowledgement, needs {{APPROVER}}'s OK for that message. Nobody writes to the
  client directly.

## Data and confidentiality

- `docs/client/` ({{CLIENT_SOURCES}}) is **confidential and not versioned**. The discovery cites it by document and
  page, without copying its content.
- Internal use only: {{INTERNAL_ONLY}}.
- In the org and in `data/`, **synthetic data only**.
